package cajeta.io.net.dns;

import cajeta.lang.String;
import cajeta.io.net.SocketAddress;
import cajeta.io.net.dns.ResolveFamily;

/**
 * The **name-resolution backend** a [`DnsCache`](DnsCache.cajeta) calls
 * on a cache **miss** (plan item **NET-2.4**).
 *
 * The cache owns the LRU + TTL bookkeeping; the `Resolver` owns the
 * one thing the cache deliberately knows nothing about — *how a name
 * actually turns into addresses*. Separating the two is what makes the
 * cache testable without a network: production wires
 * [`SystemResolver`](SystemResolver.cajeta) (which drives the NET-2.2
 * blocking [`Dns.resolve`](Dns.cajeta) `getaddrinfo` path), while a
 * test injects a **counting** resolver and asserts that a second
 * lookup *inside the TTL* never calls through — the
 * `DnsTests.cacheHitSkipsSecondLookup` acceptance ("no second
 * `getaddrinfo`; verified via an injectable resolver counter").
 *
 * ## Contract
 *
 * A single method, mirroring the family-filtered
 * [`Dns.resolve(host, port, family)`](Dns.cajeta) overload minus the
 * port (the cache keys on `(host, family)` and bakes a caller-supplied
 * port at the surface, exactly as [`Dns`](Dns.cajeta) does — a port is
 * not part of *what was resolved*, only *what the caller asked to dial*):
 *
 *   - **success** → a freshly owned, **non-empty** `SocketAddress[]`.
 *   - **failure** → throws (the same
 *     [`NetException`](../NetException.cajeta) family
 *     [`Dns.resolve`](Dns.cajeta) raises). A throwing resolver is the
 *     cache's signal to record (or refuse to record) a **negative**
 *     result — see [`DnsCache.resolve`](DnsCache.cajeta).
 *
 * The returned array's ownership transfers to the cache, which holds it
 * as the canonical **port-0** value for the TTL window. That array is
 * never handed out: [`DnsCache.resolve`](DnsCache.cajeta) returns a
 * freshly built, port-baked `#SocketAddress[]` on every hit and miss
 * alike (see `bakePort`), so each result is the caller's own to keep,
 * mutate and free — received with `#=`, per the forced-transfer stance.
 */
public interface Resolver {

    /**
     * Resolve `host` under the `family` filter, returning every matching
     * endpoint with **port 0** (the cache bakes the real port at its
     * surface). Returns a non-empty owned array on success; throws a
     * [`NetException`](../NetException.cajeta) on any failure.
     *
     * @param host   the hostname or numeric IP literal to resolve.
     * @param family the address-family filter (`V4_ONLY` / `V6_ONLY` /
     *               `BOTH`).
     * @return a freshly owned, non-empty array of port-0 endpoints.
     */
    public #SocketAddress[] resolve(String host, ResolveFamily family);
}
